fix(sprint): implement pagination support for Jira API sprint fetching

The sprint list command was missing sprints due to API pagination not being handled.
The Jira API returns paginated results (default 50 items per page), but the application
was only fetching the first page and ignoring subsequent pages.

This fix implements comprehensive pagination support:

- Modified GetSprints method to handle paginated responses using isLast, startAt, and maxResults
- Added proper URL parameter handling for pagination queries
- Implemented iterative fetching until all pages are retrieved
- Added comprehensive test coverage for pagination scenarios including multi-page responses
- Fixed test timeouts by ensuring mock responses include required pagination fields

The missing sprints (Loki, Iron Man, Star-Lord, Spiderman) were located on the second page
of API results (items 51-55 out of 55 total). With this fix, the Q2 2025 sprint count
increased from 4 to 8 sprints, ensuring all relevant sprints are properly displayed.

Coverage: 82.1% overall, 100% for new pagination code
Tests: All 1059 tests passing, no linting issues
